From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:28:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] test(mcp): refresh the read-data-schema schema snapshot
 for include_unseen

The seen-events-only change added the optional `include_unseen` flag to
read-data-schema's events query but left its runtime schema snapshot as
it was; the snapshot test now records it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../unit/__snapshots__/tool-schemas/read-data-schema.json     | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/mcp/tests/unit/__snapshots__/tool-schemas/read-data-schema.json b/services/mcp/tests/unit/__snapshots__/tool-schemas/read-data-schema.json
index ebf42284ddd..f9a683ec609 100644
--- a/services/mcp/tests/unit/__snapshots__/tool-schemas/read-data-schema.json
+++ b/services/mcp/tests/unit/__snapshots__/tool-schemas/read-data-schema.json
@@ -7,6 +7,10 @@
                 {
                     "additionalProperties": false,
                     "properties": {
+                        "include_unseen": {
+                            "description": "Also list events that are defined but were not seen in the last 30 days. By default they are left out and only counted.",
+                            "type": "boolean"
+                        },
                         "kind": {
                             "const": "events",
                             "type": "string"
-- 
